# Salary Manager — docs pipeline (Backend)

Whole-project product requirements are **canonical in the frontend repo**. This backend keeps a link only.

## Paths

| Artifact | Location |
|---|---|
| Whole-project requirements (link) | `docs/requirements/README.md` → FE `project.md` |
| BE feature requirements | `docs/requirements/features/<feature-slug>.md` |
| Architecture | `docs/architecture/<feature-slug>.md` |
| Implementation plan | `docs/plans/<feature-slug>.md` |

## Rules

- Do **not** duplicate whole-project requirements here; update the FE file via the sibling repo when product scope changes.
- Maintain **BE-specific** feature requirements under `docs/requirements/features/`.
- For cross-cutting features, also read/update FE `docs/requirements/features/<slug>.md` when that workspace is available.
- Architecture docs must name FE vs BE ownership, endpoints, and data shapes.
- Plans must list tasks with exact file paths and verification steps.
- Do not invent requirements: capture what the user approved in brainstorming.
